      "prism:coverDate": "1975-01-01",
      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "Jul",
      "dc:description": "The optimum design and rating of the drainage filter wells in lignite opencast mining are making steady progress thanks to ever better methods of analytical ground-water hydraulics. However, practical advantages of these advances are called into question, or at least limited, when the optimum design does not also result in a trouble-free operation of the wells. To deal with such problems, investigations were undertaken by the Freiberg Mining Academy, and were partly based on the already available research results concerning water management, particularly water supply and treatment. Initial results of these investigations are reported.",
