      "dc:title": "OPENCAST MINING CATCHES ON IN SOUTH AFRICA.",
      "dc:creator": "Holz P.",
      "prism:publicationName": "Coal Min Process",
      "prism:volume": "12",
      "prism:issueIdentifier": "3",
      "prism:pageRange": "44-45",
      "prism:coverDate": "1975-01-01",
      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "Mar",
      "dc:description": "Anglo Power Collieries in the Anglo American Corp. Group are partially converting their Arnot Colliery to an opencast operation. At Arnot Colliery site, technicians are currently assembling the largest dragline unit in South Africa - a Bucyrus Erie 1570 W model. The dragline with its 285-ft boom will be capable of moving 1,620,000 cu ft of overburden per day in a sidecasting operation. It will ship 115 cu ft of overburden for every ton of coal mined.",
