      "prism:coverDate": "1970-01-01",
      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "Oct",
      "dc:description": "This paper is an attempt at the presentation of the opencast coal mining technique as it prevails in the Soviet Union, one of the leading coal producing countries in the world today. Considering the phenomenal development in the coal mining industry of that country, production from opencast mining accounted for about 24% of total coal production during the year 1967. With the increased application of the soviet equipment in India, a brief survey of the Soviet machines, mechanization and technique should be of interest. Soviet practice of application of excavation and other equipment is dealt with in some detail with special reference to their operating parameters.",
