      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "May",
      "dc:description": "In parallel with underground mining, during past ten yrs rapid development of opencast mining has taken place in Poland; at present nearly 200 million tons of ore and minerals are mined by opencast methods and approximately 150 million tons by underground mining; steadily increasing depth of mined mineral deposits, increasing productive capacity of single mine up to 50 million t/yr and introduction of large capacity belt conveying are main developments illustrated in case of sulfur open pit mine near Tarnobrzeg in Central Poland, producing presently 400,000 t/yr of pure S and Turow mine, near Czechoslovakia and East German borders, producing 15 million t/yr of lignite, with installed total length of belt conveyors amounting to 100 km.",
